2-4a10-993a-6c827ca0194e")) (text "Shared completion\nresistors (fixed)\n-> A1 of BOTH ADCs" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 360.68 173.99 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "aaa08e21-b957-44bc-8632-a16401a765ff")) (text "NOTES\n1. Each half-bridge head (2 gauges) plugs into a 3-pin header: V (+3V3), SIG (mid-point), GND. The two fixed 350R\n   completion resistors are shared; their mid-point (ADS_REF) goes to A1 of both ADCs. Excitation is the ADC's own VIN, so\n   VREF_SUPPLY is ratiometric: no Ref+/Ref- wiring.\n2. 3V3 comes ONLY from the on-board LDO (from the loom's 5 V): cable voltage drop and the main board's switching noise do\n   not reach the bridges or the ADC reference. The ADC logic lines (SDA/SCL) are pulled up by the ADS122C04 breakouts to\n   this 3V3 and are 3.3 V logic: the master must not drive them above 3.6 V.\n3. Input filters are optional: with the 0R links and no capacitor fitted there is none (original behaviour). Fit 1k in each\n   link and 100nF across A0-A1 for about an 800 Hz low-pass.\n4. ADS #2: bridge one address jumper on its back (resulting address unconfirmed; the main board's firmware scans at boot).\n5. Use shielded twisted cable for the gauge wires, shield to GND at this board only." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 277 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "64b300da-3ab5-4322-9d0d-27fad891285e")) (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1"))) (embedded_fonts no))